course: dictionary
lesson: 15521
title: Big words, big changes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how much something changes. Substantially is a formal word that means by a large amount, or a lot. «Prices rose substantially this year.» The prices went up by a lot, so substantially tells you the rise was big.
explain: Substantially can also mean mainly, or in most ways. «The two stories are substantially the same.» The stories are not identical in every detail, but they match in most ways. Look at the clues: the word same tells you they are alike, and substantially tells you they are almost, but not quite, exactly alike.
explain: Test your guess by swapping in a plain word such as a lot, greatly or mostly. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Substantially is a formal word, so you will meet it most in news, reports and exams.
fact: Substantially is an adverb. Its adjective is substantial.
fact: «Substantially» means by a large amount: «prices rose substantially».
fact: «Substantially» can also mean mainly or in most ways: «the two stories are substantially the same».
fact: Plain words for substantially include a lot, much, greatly and mostly.
fact: In maths, «substantially more» means much more, but it does not give an exact number.
exercise: «The price of bread rose substantially last year.» What does substantially mean here? | Without any money at all | By a tiny amount, hardly noticed | *By a large amount | In a loud voice
exercise: «The two drawings are substantially the same.» Which word could replace substantially here? | *mostly | suddenly | never
exercise: Find and copy one word that means about the same as substantially. | *greatly | tiny | slowly | silent
test: «Our class raised substantially more money than last year.» What does substantially mean here? | Not at all | *By a large amount | Very quietly | Only just
test: Ben says, «The two maps are substantially the same.» Which is the best meaning? | *Mostly the same, in most ways | Very old | Completely different | Written in pencil
exam: «Sales fell substantially after the new shop opened.» Which word best replaces substantially? | slightly | *greatly | quietly | never
